 "text": "Hi, how have you been? You can still do them, but they' look silly without a tent. Which way are you parked, facing? Find a clear space you have right of stay, and set up before it gets dark. Stick each leg in and lock them, then get out and enjoy the fire. Not really, tents are designed for this. Each leg of a stake tent is much stronger than you need. Keep the poles out of the bag and hand warmer ready, just in case. Try asking her to pick the longest ones. People usually underestimate how much they notice. Then give her the shortest and some sticks that have already gone in. People appreciate being part of the decision.",
